zreader 0.5.1: targeted heavy-page ghosting control (not deployed)

Baseline
  Captured v0.5 executable SHA256:
  05f6990562646e15d021cc235f001851f0eb46ea5766b545259b8d51fdf7eabf
  This matches the deployed 05f69905 baseline supplied in the task.

Dark mode / driver findings
  Angel confirmed intentional hardware dark mode. It remains respected.
  This code renders black-on-white bytes and never software-inverts the buffer.
  No FBIOPUT_VSCREENINFO, SET_NIGHTMODE, inversion flags or procfs writes added.
  Local FBInk's eink/mtk-kindle.h documents grayscale=2 as 8-bit hardware inversion;
  fbink.c:2598-2604 documents the driver's preference for this inherited state.
  Startup now logs v.grayscale and whether it is 2, without changing it.
  Current physical procfs/framebuffer state was NOT inspected from the box:
  no Mac/Kindle command was run and no inversion behaviour was changed.
  Existing global fast flags are retained. FBInk's MTK header documents their
  heuristic for DU/GL16/GC16_PARTIAL, not forced GC16 FULL, so they need not be
  disabled for the new clean requests.

Root of the refresh-policy defect
  v0.5 already paired REAGL with the FULL update_mode value. That does NOT turn
  REAGL into a flashing waveform. It stayed REAGL even after a dark cover.
  The policy had no per-page darkness/image or outgoing-pixel history, and no
  periodic refresh control in the provided source. GC16 was effectively limited
  to opening/manual refresh/exit. The new policy explicitly chooses waveform 2
  (GC16) AND FULL, with full-screen geometry and GC16 histogram fallbacks.

Implementation
  1. Workers collect image footprints during the existing display-list draw.
     A 32-pixel union grid avoids double-counting overlaps. This is conservative
     bounding coverage: clipping/transparency can overestimate coverage.
  2. A fixed step-8 sample grid measures mean ink, dark-pixel fraction and
     midtone fraction. Cached metrics accompany each of the 14 pixel slots.
  3. A retained 33,708-byte grid records the submitted base page, not transient
     menu/selection overlays. Transitions measure <80 -> >192 and the reverse.
  4. Heavy = image coverage >=25% plus ink >=12% or midtones >=2.5%; or mean
     ink >=25% / dark fraction >=30%; or either large-transition fraction >=14%.
     Covers and opening/context refreshes also clean. Both transition directions
     keep the policy correct when the driver inverts physical light/dark.
  5. Normal text keeps REAGL, two workers, directional prefetch and cached pixels.
     The requested periodic setting defaults to every 8 turns since a clean;
     Off / 4 / 8 / 16 menu choices persist in settings.json. Off disables only
     periodic text cleans, never heavy/context cleans. --full-refresh overrides
     settings for one session. Startup logs the effective setting.
  6. Opening books and returning from menus/library force full-screen GC16 FULL.
     Dismissing annotation/selection popups on pages with images does likewise.
  7. Opaque axis-aligned images get 4x4 ordered dithering to 16 grayscale levels,
     immediately after that image draw. A pre-draw snapshot ensures untouched
     pixels, including any text outside PDF clips, are NOT modified. Subsequent
     text/vector operations retain MuPDF antialiasing. Masks/transparency/rotation
     are skipped; images drawn into transparency-group buffers may be unchanged.
     No aggressive grayscale contrast stretch; black/white endpoints preserved.
     --no-image-dither is available.
  8. No blind two-stage white/black flash: no device measurement justifies adding
     one yet. GC16 FULL physically clearing the reported residue needs playtest.

